# Title: Python Initiated Connection
# ID: bef0bc5a-b9ae-425d-85c6-7b2d705980c6
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: frack113
# Date: 2021-12-10
# Tags: attack.discovery, attack.t1046
# Description: Detects a Python process initiating a network connection. While this often relates to package installation, it can also indicate a potential malicious script communicating with a C&C server.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog ((Initiated="true" AND (process_path="*\\python*" AND process_path="*.exe*")) AND NOT (((dest_ip="127.0.0.1" AND src_ip="127.0.0.1") OR ((process_exec="*pip.exe*" AND process_exec="*install*")))) AND NOT (((parent_process_path="C:\\ProgramData\\Anaconda3\\Scripts\\conda.exe" AND (process_exec="*:\\ProgramData\\Anaconda3\\Scripts\\conda-script.py*" AND process_exec="*update*")) OR (parent_process_path="C:\\ProgramData\\Anaconda3\\python.exe" AND process_exec="*C:\\ProgramData\\Anaconda3\\Scripts\\jupyter-notebook-script.py*"))))
